PATCH 606: the rocket class -- b8d1's near offsets, the T-80's launcher 9699/96c0/9667/9af3.

board:0017.  b8d1, the type-0xf rocket init (asm 0xb8d1-0xb917), takes SI = the new object and DI =
the firer as near offsets: `mov [si+0x2b],di` stores the firer's WORD.  Ghidra's host-pointer body
stored the firer's 32-bit host address over +0x2b..+0x2e (b945/b998 read the word and the two bytes
above are the rocket's own), and the M3's launcher 8270 (patch 541) passed host pointers to match;
the port's rocket at 0xb22e diverged from the original's from step 6331 of the third full AZER1
run.  The T-80's side of the same class was Ghidra's throughout: 9699 (the trigger, `bx = 0 if
byte[di+0xb7] == 4 else 1 if byte[di+0xb8] == 4 else stc`), 96c0 (`call 9699 ; jae ; call 9667` on
the CF), 9667 (the rack arming, byte[di+bx+0xb7] = 2) and 9af3 (the launcher, the twin of 8270) --
host derefs of a near offset, a host pointer fed to b1df, the CF dropped.  All four rebuilt from
their asm in the DGROUP model.

